        {
          "id": "10896ba3-fce7-4831-82bb-9629c6f3c9cd",
          "name": "List blog posts",
          "request": {
            "name": "List blog posts",
            "description": {
              "content": "Returns a list of blog posts which the current user may access\n## Pagination\nUse `page[number]` and `page[size]` parameters to paginate results:\n### Get first page of 10 items\n* `GET /v1/blog_posts[number]=1&page[size]=10`\n### Get second page of 25 items\n* `GET /v1/blog_posts[number]=2&page[size]=25`\n\n## Sparse Fields\nUse the `fields[blog_posts]` parameter to request only specific attributes:\n### Only return title attribute\n* `GET /v1/blog_posts?fields[blog_posts]=title`\n\n## Sorting\nUse the `sort` parameter to sort the results:\n### Sort by published_at in descending order\n* `GET /v1/blog_posts?sort=-published_at&fields[blog_posts]=title`\n\n## Filters\nUse the `filter[site_id]` parameter to get blog posts for a specific site:\n### Get blog posts for site with ID 123\n* `GET /v1/blog_posts?filter[site_id]=123`\n\nList of attributes that may be used to filter: title, content, slug, page_title, page_description, published_at, created_at, updated_at, image_url, image_alt_text, tags\n\nThe filter param uses the following syntax: `filter[attribute_name_suffix]` with suffix for comparison:\n* `eq` for equals\n* `cont` for contains\n* `not_eq` for not equals\n* `not_cont` for not contains\n* `start` for starts with\n* `end` for ends with\n\nFor example:\n* `GET /v1/blog_posts?filter[title_start]=Announcing`\n* `GET /v1/blog_posts?filter[title_cont]=Announcing`\n",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "blog_posts"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Sort order, use: title for descending order use '-' e.g. &sort=-title"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "page[number]",
                  "value": "<integer>"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "page[size]",
                  "value": "<integer>",
                  "description": "Number of documents"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "fields[blog_posts]",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Partial attributes as specified, e.g. fields[blog_posts]=title"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "filter[title_cont]",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Filter by title contains, for example ?filter[title_cont]=hello"
                }
              ],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/vnd.api+json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{bearerToken}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
